A school in Chitungwiza records the times (in seconds) of the athletes in a 100 m race. The times are stored in a binary search tree made of `Node` objects. The Python program below builds the tree by inserting the times 14, 9, 17, 12, 8, 15 and 20, in that order. Smaller times go to the left of a node and other times to the right.

```python
class Node:
    def __init__(self, time):
        self.time = time
        self.left = None
        self.right = None

def insert(node, time):
    if node is None:
        return Node(time)
    if time < node.time:
        node.left = insert(node.left, time)
    else:
        node.right = insert(node.right, time)
    return node

def in_order(node, result):
    if node is not None:
        in_order(node.left, result)
        result.append(node.time)
        in_order(node.right, result)

root = None
for time in (14, 9, 17, 12, 8, 15, 20):
    root = insert(root, time)
```

You will write further functions for this program. Assume that the code above is already in your program.

